beam_rt: attribute the region-reclaim verification hit and name the unknown boxed header

The post-move verification reported a bare bool, so a hit said only "a live word
stands in an old region" without naming the holder; and the reachability walk
refused an unknown boxed header with a static str only, so the offending header
word was unrecoverable.

- eval/reclaim.rs: Walk::UnknownHeader { header, term } at the walk's _ => arm,
  plus Walk::{reason, header, is_complete}. reason() answers the same strings the
  refusal sites answered before, so every recorded reason is byte-identical;
  is_complete() is the single predicate every caller branches on, so an
  UnknownHeader stays a refusal everywhere (decline/retain/keep-both).
- runtime/reclaim.rs: RegionReclaimStats::{reclaim_last_decline_header,
  store_move_hit} + MoveHitOwner { Family(RootFamily, usize), CallerSlot(usize),
  OutsideCorpus }; the header field is set only on the unknown-header path and
  cleared by decline().
- runtime/reclaim/compact.rs: verification_hits -> verification_owner, attributing
  the first reproduction in the caller's slots then family-by-family over
  for_each_root_family_mut (hit path only). R_VERIFY_HIT and KeptBoth unchanged.
- runtime/retention.rs: store_move_hit{,_family,_slot} + reclaim_last_decline_header
  on RetentionStats and in the one-line [rt-mem] Display.
- runtime/roots.rs: RootFamily is pub -- the vocabulary the diagnostic reports in.

